Experiment 5 — C Control Structure Syntax
Aim

To write a program to recognize valid control structure syntax of C, such as for, while, if-else, if-else-if, and switch-case, using FLEX and BISON.

Algorithm

FLEX:

Start the FLEX program.
Define tokens for control keywords:
if
else
for
while
switch
case
default
Define patterns for identifiers and numbers.
Define tokens for braces, parentheses, colon, semicolon, and relational operators.
Pass the recognized tokens to BISON.

BISON:
6. Define grammar rules for:

if
if-else
while
for
switch-case
Define grammar rules for conditions and relational operators.
Start parsing using yyparse().
If the input matches the grammar, print Valid control structure syntax.
Otherwise, report Invalid control structure syntax.
Stop.
Pseudocode
START

Define tokens:
    IF, ELSE, FOR, WHILE
    SWITCH, CASE, DEFAULT
    ID, NUM
    Braces, Parentheses, Colon, Semicolon
    Relational operators

Read C control structure

Identify tokens using FLEX

Pass tokens to BISON

Check grammar:

IF input is IF statement:
    Validate condition and statement

ELSE IF input is IF-ELSE:
    Validate condition and both statements

ELSE IF input is WHILE:
    Validate condition and loop body

ELSE IF input is FOR:
    Validate initialization, condition,
    increment/decrement and body

ELSE IF input is SWITCH:
    Validate case/default structure

IF grammar is valid:
    Print "Valid control structure syntax"
ELSE:
    Print "Invalid control structure syntax"

STOP
